RA9_PROPOSAL	rules	NASAM	VHPScan	Strong	Current mapped Patriot automatic acquisition retains a still legal target, otherwise chooses the nearest visible hostile damageable target by squared Extent gap then SimId. No virtual-health reservation, recovery clock or repair-reset state is maintained; several batteries can send delayed missiles at the same living aircraft despite already lethal pending fire. This is an explicit current-model gameplay difference from documented Strong, not original-engine nonuse. Actual impact damage, visibility, power and delayed-missile provenance remain independently required.	source=rules:NASAM:VHPScan;model-census=e13f8cb1a7cbf0e939c4903325920057a5d2215803b7bbcc6854ea101055e8fe;original-closure=3f993d84ec5ee9e77643209623121c60c4e241cb7bcc096486d846030439ead7	ra9.compositor.special.Vhp.NASAM.VHPScan
